\p{Which changes preserve the model while transporting its equations,
expectations and retained law? A symmetry preserves the specified data;
it transports observables rather than fixing every observable function
individually. Relabellings of a finite carrier are discrete permutations,
although finite-dimensional field fibres can also admit continuous
internal actions. Here endpoint transport, coherent edge reversals and
preserved weights control incidence and operator transport; the half-turn
of the alternating cycle gives a concrete action. With compatible
perfect pairings and transport of the chosen retained split, the
observable functionals and marginal transport as well. The
[duality](fdip-001F), [split-map](fdip-001T) and
[normalized-functional](fdip-0021) conventions are assumed.}

\p{A [finite background](fdip-000G) records the supplied data.
The [Gaussian integral](fdip-002T) and [marginal theorem](fdip-000E)
identify transported functionals with normalized laws. Fixed labels,
broken weights and nonstable partitions give different failures.
The [trace ratio](fdip-003H) distinguishes weighted cycles even under
a broader comparison allowing positive scaling. These examples prepare
[enriched-background comparisons](fdip-001E), where the permitted
arrows must specify exactly what survives.}

